  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "The value of\n\n\\[\\dfrac{1}{10} + \\dfrac{2}{20} + \\dfrac{3}{30}\\]\n\nis",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.1\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.123\\)",
    "C": "\\(0.2\\)",
    "D": "\\(0.3\\)",
    "E": "\\(0.6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Reduce the fractions first so that all three terms are expressed in tenths. Dividing the numerator and denominator of \\(2/20\\) by \\(2\\), and those of \\(3/30\\) by \\(3\\), gives\n\\[\n\\frac1{10}+\\frac2{20}+\\frac3{30}\n=\\frac1{10}+\\frac1{10}+\\frac1{10}\n=\\frac3{10}=0.3.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
